  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/poecilia-caucana-2/",
      "html": "<p>With an overall length of 3–5 cm the Cauca Molly (Poecilia caucana), originating from Colombia, Venezuela and Panama, belongs to the smaller livebearers. Remarkable in males are the yellow-orange dorsal fin, a violet metallic shine along the body and the orange band in the proximal part of the caudal fin.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/poecilia-caucana-2/",
      "html": "<p>The water values (pH 8.2–8.6, conductivity 360 and 420 µS/cm), based on different places where the animals are found in the area of the Rio Cauca, make them suitable aquarium inhabitants for most Central European tap waters. These fish appreciate higher temperatures between 26 and 28°C.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/poecilia-caucana-2/",
      "html": "<p>As an algae eater the Cauca molly is constantly on the search for food. All usual kinds of fish food are greedily eaten.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/poecilia-caucana-2/",
      "html": "<p>With appropriate care a new generation will appear sooner or later.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/poecilia-caucana-2/",
      "html": "<p>The fish currently available are bred ones from Southeast Asia.</p>"
    }
  ],
